## Timing of one step at batch 1

{% set t = s.time_by_cause_batch1_ms %}
| | time | share |
|---|---|---|
| passes over weight banks, with the per-operation latency | {{ n(t.scan, 3) }} ms | {{ pct(t.scan / s.batch1.step_ms) }} |
| full attention: arithmetic | {{ n(t.attn_compute, 3) }} ms | {{ pct(t.attn_compute / s.batch1.step_ms) }} |
| full attention: KV fetch | {{ n(t.attn_fetch, 3) }} ms | {{ pct(t.attn_fetch / s.batch1.step_ms) }} |
| hops between tiles | {{ n(t.hop, 3) }} ms | {{ pct(t.hop / s.batch1.step_ms) }} |
| step boundary, sampler | {{ n(t.fixed, 3) }} ms | {{ pct(t.fixed / s.batch1.step_ms) }} |
| **step** | **{{ n(s.batch1.step_ms, 3) }} ms** | {{ n(s.batch1.tok_s_user, -1) }} tok/s per user |

A weight operation takes {{ n(1e6 * (NK.s_op_time), 2) }} µs in all. That is not a design target: it is the whole
time per weight operation that a published wafer-scale SRAM machine shows on Llama 3.1 8B
([06](06_simulator.md)). S's own bank pass ({{ n(S.t_scan_us, 2) }} µs) is inside it. A design that needed only
half again its own pass would be
{{ x((U.tornado.rows | selectattr("parameter", "equalto", "S per-operation latency") | first).speed_batch1_low / TB.speed_batch1, 1) }}
faster than the figure reported.

Because every layer has its own tile, requests are pipelined: while one request is in layer 20,
another can be in layer 3. That is why throughput scales with batch until the shared attention tile
saturates ([04](04_results.md), section 4).

## Power

| state | weight banks | logic and clock | links, idle | KV memory | host | total |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| idle, managed (banks in retention, lanes clock-gated) | {{ n(S.static_w_managed.storage_leakage, 0) }} W | {{ n(S.static_w_managed.logic_and_clock, -1) }} W | {{ n(S.static_w_managed.links_idle, -1) }} W | {{ n(S.static_w_managed.kv_memory, 0) }} W | {{ n(S.static_w_managed.host, 0) }} W | **{{ n(S.static_w_managed.total, -1) }} W** |
| idle, unmanaged (full voltage, clocks running) | {{ n(S.static_w_unmanaged.storage_leakage, 0) }} W | {{ n(S.static_w_unmanaged.logic_and_clock, -1) }} W | {{ n(S.static_w_unmanaged.links_idle, -1) }} W | {{ n(S.static_w_unmanaged.kv_memory, 0) }} W | {{ n(S.static_w_unmanaged.host, 0) }} W | **{{ n(S.static_w_unmanaged.total, -1) }} W** |

| serving | system power |
|---|---|
| one request, 8K context | {{ n(s.batch1.watts, -1) }} W |
| {{ S.busy.batch }} requests, 32K context | {{ n(S.busy.watts, -2) }} W |

- **SRAM leakage is small once managed.** Measured leakage of a 3 nm macro at 25 °C is 27.5 pW per bit
  (sram-3nm-macro): {{ n(0.22 * S.area.resident_gb, 0) }} W for this model. We multiply by 3 for
  operating temperature (assumption; no hot figure is public) and hold idle banks at a retention
  voltage that cuts it to {{ pct(S_HW.power.retention_factor) }} (published range 5% to 31%;
  sram-retention).
- **Idle logic is the larger term**: {{ S_HW.power.logic_static_w_per_die }} W per die managed,
  {{ S_HW.power.logic_static_w_per_die_unmanaged }} W unmanaged (assumptions, swept 1 to 15 W).
- **Power density is low.** Fully busy, the system draws about {{ n(S.busy.w_per_die, 0) }} W per die,
  {{ n(S.busy.w_per_cm2, 1) }} W/cm². A B300 is {{ n(G_HW.tdp_w, 0) }} W in one package. MDS-1
  can be air-cooled; its difficulty is the number of dies, not heat.

## Packaging, power delivery, cooling

- **Tiles.** About {{ n(S.area.dies_per_tile, 0) }} large dies on one fan-out or interposer tile
  ({{ S_HW.tile_dies_max }} is the assumed limit; a layer spans more than one tile). Die-to-die links inside a
  tile are short-reach, {{ S_HW.power.d2d_pj_per_bit }} pJ/bit (d2d-energy). Packaging and test are costed at
  {{ usd(S_HW.cost.package_test_usd_per_die) }} per die, built from the same sourced parts as the HBM chip's
  package (cowos-cost); the attention tile's HBM packages are costed as the HBM chip's.
- **Between tiles.** 72 lanes of 112G serial links per neighbour, {{ n(S_HW.link_bw / 1e9, 0) }} GB/s,
  {{ n(S_HW.hop_latency * 1e9, 0) }} ns per hop including error correction (ucie-targets, with margin;
  swept 0.1 to 2 µs).
- **System.** {{ S.area.tiles }} tiles plus the attention tile: several chassis, not one board.
  Boards, power delivery, cooling and chassis are costed at {{ usd(S_HW.cost.system_usd_per_die) }} per
  die (assumption).
- **Power delivery** at {{ pct(S_HW.power.vr_efficiency) }} efficiency (assumption, as MDA-1).

