## MDF-1: what changes when the weights are fixed

| | MDS-1 | MDF-1 |
|---|---|---|
| weight storage | SRAM, {{ S_HW.area.mm2_per_mib_sram }} mm²/MiB, plus multiplier lanes | mask-programmed, {{ F_HW.area.mm2_per_mib_rom }} mm²/MiB including arithmetic |
| dies | {{ S.area.dies }} | {{ F.area.dies }} |
| distinct die designs | {{ S.cost.distinct_die_designs }} | {{ F.cost.distinct_die_designs }} |
| tiles | {{ S.area.tiles }} | {{ F.area.tiles }} |
| time per weight operation | {{ n(1e6 * NK.s_op_time, 2) }} µs (a published SRAM wafer machine's) | {{ n(CL.latency_for_f_total_us, 2) }} µs (a shipped fixed-weight die's) |
| idle weight storage power | {{ n(S.static_w_managed.storage_leakage, 0) }} W | {{ n(F.static_w_managed.storage_leakage, 0) }} W |
| new model version | load weights | {{ F.cost.distinct_die_designs }} dies × {{ F_HW.cost.unique_mask_layers }} mask layers: {{ usd(F.cost.unique_mask_usd / 1e6, 1) }}M and a fab cycle |

MDF-1's density comes from one shipped chip: 8B parameters at 3 and 6 bits on an 815 mm² N6 die
(taalas-hc1), scaled by 1.5 to N4P-class (assumption). Its latency is what that chip's published
speed implies. Both are single-die results at 8B parameters carried to {{ F.area.dies }} dies; nothing
public confirms they carry. The vendor's own figure for a model of this class is labeled a simulation
by the vendor.

## What has not been validated

- No floorplan, no place-and-route of a die, no timing closure of a {{ S.scan_rows }}-row bank at
  {{ n(S.f_clk / 1e9, 1) }} GHz.
- The pooled attention engine ({{ n(S_HW.attn_peak_full / 1e15, 0) }} PFLOP/s) is sized by assumption, and it caps the system's throughput. Queueing in front of it is not modeled.
- A {{ S.area.dies }}-die system has {{ S.area.tiles }} tiles and their links to bring up, test and keep
  running. Availability is not modeled.
- Wake from retention in {{ n(S_HW.wake_latency * 1e9, 0) }} ns across a whole bank.
- The weight loader, error correction and repair flow.
